  "body": "The external acceptance report (R8) recorded a confirmed defect: `main` described the product as `CANDIDATE_ONLY` / `Not released` / \"installs one console script, `sbl-todo`\" while two releases exist and `pyproject.toml` installs three console scripts.\n\nThis PR is docs and governance records only:\n\n- `README.md`: status section names the released pre-release line (`v0.1.0-foundation-preview`, `v0.1.1rc1`), keeps the non-production / non-independent-acceptance ceiling, and lists `sbl-todo` / `sbl-stack` / `sbl-harness` as installed.\n- `docs/RUN_CONFORMANCE.md`: the conformance command that actually runs on this host (`PYTHONPATH=src`; `--timeout` does not exist here), and the rule that a count is only valid together with its tree state.\n- `openspec/changes/far-r12-20261021/`: proposal + tasks for this round, including the five open owner decisions.\n- `_governance/round-20261021-r12-far/`: FAR deviation study (D-01..D-16) and the bounded-writer receipt, including the honest record of the writer lane failing its arm check (`ERR_NO_ARM_EMITTED_NONCE`) and the manual byte review that replaced it.\n\nNo change to `sbl_core/`, `sbl_sp/`, `sbl_cli/`, `contracts/`, `tests/` or `tools/`. No native effect, no host install, no independent acceptance, no full-contract pass, no completion percentage.",
